              "textField": "Benzodiazepines are drugs that bind onto the inhibitory Gaba receptor and potentiate the actions of that receptor. Do not take for long periods of time because tolerance develops. Drug(s) that fit this description include *Clonazepam, lorazepam and diazepam*\n*Gabapentin and Pregabalin* Inhibit calcium into the presynaptic neurons. Indicated for partial seizures (not generalized seizures) and neuropathic pain. \n*Carbamazepine* Decrease sodium into the presynaptic neuron. Indicated for focal and generalised seizures but can cause bone marrow malfunction so frequent blood tests should be performed. \n*Valproic acid (valproate)* Decrease(s) sodium into the presynaptic neuron and increases the affinity of GABA in the post synaptic neurons. Treats partial and generalised seizures and stabilizes mood."
